Z||000000||BENGAL4||11-23-1999||11:15 AM||||I bought an Ocelot system from the Fiero Store and when I installed it, I found out that the pipe ends were not expanded so it would fit up. I had to take them to a muffler shop and have them expand them. Well it seems that the pipe that connects to the cat is to big and I have a slight leak. Last night it came loose with the clamop still attached.<P>My question is, how do I seal this up? Do I put 2 clamps on it? Has anyone had this problem? I also thought about putting a reducer sleeve between the 2 connections to make a tighter fit up. What do you guys think? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||lennyb4||11-23-1999||02:30 PM||||I recently put a custom exhast on my 87. I basicly had the same problem. The easiest fix, i took it to a muffler shop and for $20 they welded all of the joints together.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||11-23-1999||04:56 PM||||I vote for the muffler shop welding them too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GT||11-23-1999||07:08 PM||||I would weld also.  I have the OCelot system and it came apart there also.  That car of mine was louder than hell when it came apart. I took it straight to the shop and had them weld it.  ||||reg||1
